1
00:00:04,525 --> 00:00:12,525
Connect a video provider — Settings ▸ Telehealth Setup — Connect one account for the clinic, and every provider can start a visit.

2
00:00:17,902 --> 00:00:26,245
Settings ▸ Telehealth Setup holds the clinic’s video account. Connect it once, and every provider uses it.

3
00:00:26,245 --> 00:00:34,409
Four providers are supported: Google Meet, Zoom, Cisco Webex and Microsoft Teams.

4
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:44,711
Connecting is an OAuth sign-in: you approve it in the provider’s own window and no password is ever stored here.

5
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:55,648
Google Meet is already connected on this clinic — you can see the account it is connected as.

6
00:00:55,648 --> 00:01:01,468
Test Connection proves the token still works before a patient is waiting on it.

7
00:01:01,468 --> 00:01:07,945
If a token has expired, Reconnect re-runs the sign-in — nothing else needs changing.

8
00:01:07,945 --> 00:01:15,887
The switch on the right makes it the active provider. An account that is not connected cannot be switched on.

9
00:01:15,887 --> 00:01:28,686
That is deliberate: it stops a half-configured provider from becoming the one your visits depend on.

10
00:01:28,686 --> 00:01:35,809
And this is the payoff. Every telehealth appointment now gets a join link from that account.

11
00:01:35,809 --> 00:01:43,320
Provider and patient both open the same link. Change the provider here and every future visit follows.

12
00:01:44,729 --> 00:01:57,029
What you just did

13
00:01:57,695 --> 00:02:06,695
Health | Efficiency | Growth — More in the Getting Started series — the next video is linked on screen.
